      "narration": "Uxbridge sends the Household and Union Brigades down the slope into d'Erlon's disordered columns; the Scots Greys, Sergeant Ewart among them, capture the eagle of the 45th Line, and the brigades ride on toward the grande batterie. Out of control and blown, they are caught by French lancers and cuirassiers. About 3,000 of d'Erlon's men are lost and his corps needs until about 16:00 to re-form, but the heavy cavalry is badly mauled and the Union Brigade loses its commander, Ponsonby.",
